.TH MENTA\-SOURCES 1 "October 2026" "menta-sources" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
menta\-sources, software\-properties\-gtk \- configure the software sources of Debian
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B menta\-sources
.RB [ \-n ]
.br
.B software\-properties\-gtk
.RB [ \-n ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B menta\-sources
(Software Sources) configures where APT downloads software from.
It asks for administrator privileges with
.BR pkexec (1).
.PP
The official Debian repositories are written to
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/debian.sources
in deb822 format. Their mirror, components (main, contrib, non\-free,
non\-free\-firmware), update suites (security, updates, backports,
proposed\-updates, experimental), source code and debug symbol repositories
can be chosen in the "Debian Software" tab.
.PP
Official entries found in
.I /etc/apt/sources.list
or other one\-line files are moved to
.IR debian.sources ,
after saving a copy of the original files in
.IR /var/backups/menta\-sources/ .
.PP
Third party repositories and their keys are managed in the "Other Software"
and "Authentication" tabs. PPAs are not supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-update
Don't offer to reload the package information after a change; exit with
status 1 if the sources were modified instead. Used by package managers such as
.BR synaptic (8).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/menta\-sources/<codename>/menta\-sources.conf
Description of each supported Debian release: default mirror, available
components and suites.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sources.list (5),
.BR add\-apt\-repository (1),
.BR apt (8)
